WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.900
A fallen beam blocks the mill lane. A pole over a log makes a lever.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.350
Log in the middle: your push is as big as the lift, and both ends move the same distance.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:16.900
Roll the log close to the beam: half the push, but your end moves twice as far.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:24.900
Half the push, twice the distance. In this model, push times the distance pushed down stays the same.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:33.900
A ramp four times as long as it is high: a quarter of the force, four times the distance. (A model: no friction.)

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Less push, longer path. Real machines have friction, so you need more push than this.
